---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const areas = ['Communication and language','Personal, social and emotional development','Physical development','Literacy','Mathematics','Understanding the world','Expressive arts and design'];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en-GB"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="How The Wonder Years Day Nursery supports learning through the EYFS, Birth to 5 Matters, observations and preparation for school."/><title>Learning and Development | The Wonder Years Day Nursery</title><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}styles/global.css`}/></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="wireframe-banner">Learning and Development wireframe · Content and image placement for review</div><header class="site-header"><div class="container header-inner"><a class="brand" href={base}><span class="logo-placeholder">LOGO</span><span>The Wonder Years<br/><small>Day Nursery</small></span></a><nav class="main-nav"><a href={`${base}about/`}>About us</a><a href={`${base}rooms/`}>Our rooms</a><a href={`${base}learning-development/`} aria-current="page">Learning &amp; development</a><a href={`${base}fees-funding/`}>Fees &amp; funding</a><a href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact</a></nav></div></header><main id="main"><section class="section hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Learning and development</p><h1>Learning built around your child</h1><p class="lead">Our curriculum follows the Early Years Foundation Stage and is informed by Birth to 5 Matters. Through play, exploration and warm relationships, children are supported to build confidence and make progress at their own pace.</p><a class="button" href={`${base}contact/`}>Arrange a visit</a></div><div class="image-placeholder hero-image"><span>Learning image placeholder</span><small>Genuine photograph of a child engaged in an activity</small></div></div></section><section class="section section-muted"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Our curriculum</p><h2>A connected approach to learning</h2><p class="section-intro">Young children learn across several areas at once. Our curriculum creates opportunities for meaningful, connected learning through everyday experiences, play and interaction.</p><div class="benefits-grid">{areas.map((area,index)=><article class="benefit-card"><span class="icon-placeholder">{index+1}</span><h3>{area}</h3></article>)}</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container split-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Observation and planning</p><h2>Following each child’s interests</h2><p>Children are observed by their key person and the wider nursery team. These observations help staff understand what interests each child, the skills they are developing and what their next steps may be.</p><p>The team uses this understanding to plan activities and experiences around the child’s interests and development.</p></div><div class="image-placeholder landscape"><span>Observation and play image placeholder</span></div></div></section><section class="section section-accent"><div class="container split-grid reverse"><div class="image-placeholder landscape"><span>School preparation image placeholder</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Preparing for school</p><h2>Helping children approach the next step with confidence</h2><p>In Grasshoppers, older children are supported as they prepare for school. During the final term, staff gather information about each child’s new school, talk to them about the change and, where possible, invite new teachers into the nursery.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}rooms/`}>Explore our rooms</a></div></div></section><section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><h2>Come and see learning in action</h2><p>Meet the team, explore the rooms and talk about your child’s interests, development and individual needs.</p><a class="button button-light" href={`${base}contact/`}>Arrange a nursery visit</a></div></section></main></body></html>